// CODE TO MOTION — Skills, Agents and pro prompts (generated)
window.CTM_AI = {"skills": [{"name": "motion-director", "ar": "المخرج الفني", "cat": "video", "desc": "Art direction for motion videos: turns a vague idea into a clear creative direction (mood, pacing, palette, type, motion language) before any code is written. Use when the user asks for a video \"that looks professional/cinematic\" or gives only a rough idea.", "dar": "يحوّل فكرتك لرؤية إخراجية واضحة (إحساس، ألوان، خطوط، إيقاع) قبل أي كود.", "file": "---\nname: motion-director\ndescription: \"Art direction for motion videos: turns a vague idea into a clear creative direction (mood, pacing, palette, type, motion language) before any code is written. Use when the user asks for a video \\\"that looks professional/cinematic\\\" or gives only a rough idea.\"\n---\n\n# Motion Director\n\nYou decide *how the video should feel* and write it down so every scene follows the same rules.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Ask at most one question if the goal or audience is missing. Otherwise assume and state the assumption.\n2. Write a **direction brief** (max 15 lines):\n   - Goal & audience · one-sentence message\n   - Mood (3 adjectives) · reference style (described in words, never \"copy X\")\n   - Palette: background, main, accent (hex) · type: heading/body font & weights\n   - Motion language: entrance style (spring damping range), exit style, transition type & length\n   - Pacing: total duration, scene count, average scene length, where the climax is\n3. Turn the brief into a scene table: `# | purpose | frames | main motion | text on screen`.\n4. Hand the table to the implementer (or implement it with the `remotion-expert` skill).\n\n## Rules of good direction\n- One main movement per scene; secondary motion must be subtler (smaller distance, lower opacity).\n- Contrast pacing: fast cuts (15–30 frames) for energy, holds (60–90 frames) for reading.\n- Text must stay on screen ≥ 1 second per 3 words.\n- Use the accent color for one thing per scene only.\n- End on the strongest frame (logo / call to action) and hold it ≥ 1.5 s.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "remotion-expert", "ar": "خبير Remotion", "cat": "video", "desc": "Builds correct, production-quality Remotion compositions: Composition registration, Sequence/Series/TransitionSeries timing, spring and interpolate, props with Zod. Use for any request to create or change a Remotion video.", "dar": "يبني فيديوهات Remotion صحيحة: التوقيت، المشاهد، الانتقالات، والقوالب بـ Zod.", "file": "---\nname: remotion-expert\ndescription: \"Builds correct, production-quality Remotion compositions: Composition registration, Sequence/Series/TransitionSeries timing, spring and interpolate, props with Zod. Use for any request to create or change a Remotion video.\"\n---\n\n# Remotion Expert\n\n## Building blocks\n| Need | Use |\n|---|---|\n| Value over time | `interpolate(frame, [a, b], [x, y], {extrapolateLeft: 'clamp', extrapolateRight: 'clamp', easing})` |\n| Natural entrance | `spring({frame: frame - delay, fps, config: {damping}})` (8 bouncy · 12 balanced · 200 no bounce) |\n| Scenes in order | `<Series>` or `<Sequence from durationInFrames>` (frame restarts at 0 inside) |\n| Transitions | `@remotion/transitions` `<TransitionSeries>`; total = Σ scenes − Σ transitions |\n| Files in public/ | `staticFile('logo.png')` with `<Img>`, `<Audio>`, `<OffthreadVideo>` |\n| Editable video | `schema` (Zod, `zColor()` from `@remotion/zod-types`) + `defaultProps` on `<Composition>` |\n| Duration from props | `calculateMetadata` on `<Composition>` |\n\n## Workflow\n1. Plan scenes and frame ranges first; write them as a comment at the top of the file.\n2. One component per scene; keep each file under ~150 lines.\n3. Register in `src/Root.tsx` with id, fps, width, height, durationInFrames.\n4. Install add-ons only with `npx remotion add <package>` so versions match.\n5. Typecheck, render stills at every scene's middle frame, fix, then render.\n\n## Common mistakes to avoid\n- Forgetting clamp → values overshoot after the range.\n- Absolutely positioned background covering normal-flow content: give content `position: 'relative'` or wrap it in `<AbsoluteFill>`.\n- Mixing versions of `remotion` and `@remotion/*` packages.\n- Using `Math.random()` — use `random('seed')` from remotion instead.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "arabic-typography", "ar": "الخطوط العربية", "cat": "design", "desc": "Correct, beautiful Arabic text in motion videos: RTL layout, font loading, mixed Arabic/English, numerals, punctuation and word-by-word animation without breaking letter joining. Use whenever on-screen text is Arabic.", "dar": "يضبط العربي في الفيديو: الاتجاه، الخطوط، الإنجليزي داخل العربي، والحركة بالكلمات.", "file": "---\nname: arabic-typography\ndescription: \"Correct, beautiful Arabic text in motion videos: RTL layout, font loading, mixed Arabic/English, numerals, punctuation and word-by-word animation without breaking letter joining. Use whenever on-screen text is Arabic.\"\n---\n\n# Arabic Typography for Video\n\n## Must-do\n- Container: `direction: 'rtl'`, `textAlign: 'right'` (or center). Flex rows: `flexDirection: 'row'` already flows right-to-left under rtl.\n- Load fonts locally: `loadFont({family: 'Cairo', url: staticFile('fonts/Cairo-900.ttf'), weight: '900'})` from `@remotion/fonts`. Good free families: Cairo, Tajawal, IBM Plex Sans Arabic, Noto Kufi Arabic, Readex Pro, Amiri (serif).\n- Animate **words, never letters**: splitting Arabic into characters breaks the joining. Split on spaces.\n- Line height 1.3–1.5 (Arabic needs more than Latin); avoid letter-spacing on Arabic.\n- English/code inside Arabic: wrap in `<span dir=\"ltr\">` so it doesn't flip.\n- Quotes: prefer «» or plain \"\" and test the render; parentheses mirror automatically.\n- Numbers: decide once — Western (123) or Arabic-Indic (١٢٣) — and keep it consistent.\n\n## Motion that suits Arabic\n- Word reveal from the right (translateX positive → 0) or from below.\n- Mask/wipe reveals going right → left.\n- Kashida-free: never stretch words with tatweel for animation.\n\n## Checklist before render\n- [ ] No reversed words or punctuation at the wrong end\n- [ ] Mixed English reads correctly\n- [ ] Font is the intended one (not a fallback) — compare a still\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "kinetic-typography", "ar": "تحريك النصوص", "cat": "design", "desc": "Kinetic typography: text that moves with rhythm — word-by-word reveals, emphasis words, scale punches, masks, and timing to voice or beat. Use for quote videos, hooks, titles and lyric-free text animations.", "dar": "تحريك النصوص بإيقاع: كلمة كلمة، إبراز الكلمة المهمة، وأقنعة ظهور.", "file": "---\nname: kinetic-typography\ndescription: \"Kinetic typography: text that moves with rhythm — word-by-word reveals, emphasis words, scale punches, masks, and timing to voice or beat. Use for quote videos, hooks, titles and lyric-free text animations.\"\n---\n\n# Kinetic Typography\n\n## Timing formula\n- Words per second on screen: 2–3 for reading, 4–5 for energy.\n- Stagger between words: 4–6 frames. Hold the full line ≥ 20 frames before it leaves.\n- Emphasis word: arrives last or with a bigger spring (damping 8) and the accent color.\n\n## Techniques (all frame-driven)\n1. **Word pop**: per word `spring({frame: frame - start - i*gap})` → opacity + translateY + scale 0.7→1.\n2. **Mask reveal**: wrapper with `overflow: hidden`, inner text translateY 100% → 0.\n3. **Scale punch**: on the key word, scale 1 → 1.15 → 1 over 8 frames with interpolate.\n4. **Line replace**: old line exits up (opacity 1→0, y 0→-40) while the new one enters from below, 6-frame overlap.\n5. **Highlight sweep**: a colored bar behind the word with scaleX 0→1 (transformOrigin right for Arabic).\n6. **Counter**: numbers via `Math.round(interpolate(...))` with tabular digits.\n\n## Layout\n- Max 2 lines on screen, max ~8 words per line in 16:9, ~4 in 9:16.\n- Keep text inside a 5% safe margin; big type (100–160 px at 1080p).\n\n## Sync to voice\nGet phrase start times (see `audio-sync`), convert seconds → frames (`Math.round(sec * fps)`), and start each line at its phrase.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "cinematic-transitions", "ar": "الانتقالات السينمائية", "cat": "video", "desc": "Cinematic scene transitions in Remotion: choosing and building fades, slides, wipes, zooms, whip-pans, light leaks and match cuts with correct timing math. Use when scenes need to connect smoothly or feel cinematic.", "dar": "انتقالات سينمائية بين المشاهد مع حساب المدة الصحيح.", "file": "---\nname: cinematic-transitions\ndescription: \"Cinematic scene transitions in Remotion: choosing and building fades, slides, wipes, zooms, whip-pans, light leaks and match cuts with correct timing math. Use when scenes need to connect smoothly or feel cinematic.\"\n---\n\n# Cinematic Transitions\n\n## Ready-made (`@remotion/transitions`)\n`fade()`, `slide({direction})`, `wipe({direction})`, `flip()`, `clockWipe({width, height})`, with `linearTiming({durationInFrames})` or `springTiming({config, durationInFrames})`.\nNewer versions also ship more presentations (for example dissolve, cross-zoom, zoom-blur, push-cut, film-burn). Check `node_modules/@remotion/transitions` or the docs for what your version has before using one.\n**Duration math:** total = sum of scene durations − sum of transition durations. Recalculate every time.\n\n## Choosing\n| Feeling | Transition | Length |\n|---|---|---|\n| Calm, elegant | fade / cross-dissolve | 15–25 f |\n| Energy, next point | slide or whip | 8–15 f |\n| Reveal / new chapter | wipe, clockWipe | 15–20 f |\n| Continuity | match cut (same shape/color position in both scenes) | 0 f |\n\n## Custom moves (frame-driven)\n- **Zoom-through**: outgoing scale 1→3 + opacity→0, incoming scale 0.6→1.\n- **Whip pan**: translateX ±120% with motion blur feel — add `filter: blur(px)` peaking mid-transition (keep ≤ 12px for render speed), or `@remotion/motion-blur`.\n- **Light leak**: an absolutely positioned radial gradient with opacity peaking at the cut.\n\n## Rules\n- Use at most 2 transition types per video.\n- Direction should follow reading direction (Arabic: content arrives from the left edge and moves right-to-left consistently).\n- Never put a transition over text people still need to read.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "3d-motion-design", "ar": "الموشن ثلاثي الأبعاد", "cat": "video", "desc": "3D elements in Remotion using @remotion/three (React Three Fiber): product spins, floating logos, 3D text and camera moves synced to frames. Use when the user asks for 3D in a Remotion video.", "dar": "عناصر ثلاثية الأبعاد في Remotion بـ @remotion/three، أو 3D خفيف بالـ CSS.", "file": "---\nname: 3d-motion-design\ndescription: \"3D elements in Remotion using @remotion/three (React Three Fiber): product spins, floating logos, 3D text and camera moves synced to frames. Use when the user asks for 3D in a Remotion video.\"\n---\n\n# 3D Motion Design\n\n## Setup\n`npx remotion add @remotion/three` then use `<ThreeCanvas width height>` from `@remotion/three` inside a composition. Inside it, regular React Three Fiber (`mesh`, lights, materials). Drive everything from `useCurrentFrame()` — do **not** use `useFrame` from R3F.\n\n## Patterns\n- **Turntable**: `rotation.y = interpolate(frame, [0, duration], [0, Math.PI * 2])`.\n- **Float**: `position.y = Math.sin(frame / 20) * 0.1`.\n- **Camera push-in**: animate camera z with spring; keep FOV constant.\n- **Logo in 3D**: extrude an SVG shape (`ExtrudeGeometry`) or put the logo image on a plane with slight rotation.\n- Lighting: one key light, one rim light in the accent color, soft ambient (0.3–0.5).\n\n## Fake 3D without three.js (lighter, faster)\nCSS `perspective` on the parent + `rotateX/rotateY/translateZ` on children; layered parallax (background moves less than foreground).\n\n## Performance\n- Keep polygon counts low; avoid real-time shadows unless needed.\n- Render a short range first: `--frames=0-60`.\n- Use `--gl=angle` (or the renderer's recommended GL option) if 3D renders black on the server.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "brand-animation", "ar": "تحريك الهوية", "cat": "design", "desc": "Animating a brand identity: logo reveals, brand intros/outros, consistent motion rules from brand colors and fonts. Use when the user gives a logo or brand guide and wants intros, outros, stingers or a motion kit.", "dar": "تحريك الهوية: كشف الشعار، مقدمات وخاتمات، وحركة توقيع ثابتة لعلامتك.", "file": "---\nname: brand-animation\ndescription: \"Animating a brand identity: logo reveals, brand intros/outros, consistent motion rules from brand colors and fonts. Use when the user gives a logo or brand guide and wants intros, outros, stingers or a motion kit.\"\n---\n\n# Brand Animation\n\n## Inputs to collect\nLogo file (SVG preferred, else transparent PNG in `public/`), brand colors (hex), fonts, tagline, tone (serious / friendly / bold).\n\n## Motion identity (write this first)\n- Signature move: one repeatable motion (e.g., spring scale with damping 10 + 20° rotation) used in every brand video.\n- Timing: intro 3–5 s, outro 4–6 s, stinger ≤ 1.5 s.\n- Easing personality: corporate → `Easing.inOut(Easing.cubic)`; playful → spring damping 8–10; luxury → slow fades 30+ frames.\n\n## Logo reveal recipes\n1. **Burst**: expanding rings in accent color → logo springs in → name below.\n2. **Draw-on** (SVG): `evolvePath` from `@remotion/paths` animates strokes, then fill fades in.\n3. **Mask wipe**: logo revealed by a moving rectangle mask.\n4. **Assemble**: logo parts (separate SVG paths) fly in from different directions with staggered springs.\n\n## Deliverables\nMake every brand video a template: props for logo, colors, tagline (Zod schema). Export intro/outro as MP4, and stingers with alpha (`--codec=prores --prores-profile=4444` or WebM VP8/VP9 with transparent background).\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "ui-animation", "ar": "تحريك الواجهات", "cat": "design", "desc": "UI and product-screen animation: app/website screenshots in device frames, cursor clicks, scrolling pages, UI elements popping in. Use for SaaS demos, app promos and feature highlights.", "dar": "تحريك لقطات التطبيقات والمواقع: إطار جوال، سكرول، مؤشر يضغط، وزوم على الميزة.", "file": "---\nname: ui-animation\ndescription: \"UI and product-screen animation: app/website screenshots in device frames, cursor clicks, scrolling pages, UI elements popping in. Use for SaaS demos, app promos and feature highlights.\"\n---\n\n# UI Animation\n\n## Building blocks\n- **Device frame**: rounded rect with border + `<Img>` of the screenshot (`objectFit: 'cover'`). Phone ~380×780 at 1080p, laptop ~1200×750.\n- **Scroll**: tall screenshot inside a fixed frame, `translateY = interpolate(frame, [a, b], [0, -(imgH - frameH)])` with `Easing.inOut`.\n- **Cursor**: an SVG arrow moving between points with spring; click = scale 1→0.85→1 + ripple circle.\n- **Zoom to feature**: scale the whole screen around the target (`transformOrigin` at the element) 1→1.8.\n- **UI pop**: rebuild key elements (buttons, cards) as real components so they can spring in on top of the screenshot.\n\n## Getting screenshots\nTake them at 2× device scale (e.g. Playwright `deviceScaleFactor: 2`) as PNG/JPEG into `public/screens/`. Hide personal data before capturing.\n\n## Pacing\nOne feature per 3–4 seconds: show → zoom → label → return. Labels short (≤ 5 words) in brand accent.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "data-visualization", "ar": "البيانات المتحركة", "cat": "design", "desc": "Animated infographics and charts in Remotion: counting numbers, bar/line/donut charts, maps-like progress, with honest scales. Use when the user wants statistics, reports or numbers turned into video.", "dar": "أرقام تعد وأعمدة ورسوم بيانية متحركة بمقاييس صادقة.", "file": "---\nname: data-visualization\ndescription: \"Animated infographics and charts in Remotion: counting numbers, bar/line/donut charts, maps-like progress, with honest scales. Use when the user wants statistics, reports or numbers turned into video.\"\n---\n\n# Data Visualization in Motion\n\n## Honesty first\n- Bars start at zero. Compare lengths only when values share a unit.\n- Show the source on screen if the numbers are real; never invent data — ask for it or label it \"example\".\n\n## Recipes\n- **Count-up**: `Math.round(interpolate(frame, [s, s+45], [0, value], {clamp, easing: Easing.out(Easing.cubic)}))`, `toLocaleString('en-US')`, tabular figures.\n- **Bars**: height = maxH × value/max × progress; stagger 10–15 frames.\n- **Line chart**: build an SVG path from points; reveal with `evolvePath(progress, d)` from `@remotion/paths` (strokeDasharray/offset).\n- **Donut**: SVG circle with `strokeDasharray = C`, `strokeDashoffset = C × (1 − share × progress)`.\n- **Highlight**: dim other elements to 30% opacity when talking about one.\n\n## Layout\nTitle top, chart center, one takeaway sentence at the end (the \"so what\"). Max 4 bars / 5 points on screen in 16:9.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "audio-sync", "ar": "مزامنة الصوت", "cat": "video", "desc": "Syncing motion to voice-over, music beats and sound effects: detecting phrase timings, converting seconds to frames, placing SFX, ducking music. Use when a video has narration or must hit beats.", "dar": "يزامن الحركة مع التعليق الصوتي والموسيقى والمؤثرات بالفريم.", "file": "---\nname: audio-sync\ndescription: \"Syncing motion to voice-over, music beats and sound effects: detecting phrase timings, converting seconds to frames, placing SFX, ducking music. Use when a video has narration or must hit beats.\"\n---\n\n# Audio Sync\n\n## Voice-over → scene timings\n1. Get the duration: `ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration -of csv=p=0 voice.mp3`.\n2. Find pauses: `ffmpeg -i voice.mp3 -af silencedetect=noise=-35dB:d=0.25 -f null -` → read `silence_end` times = phrase starts.\n3. Map each phrase to a scene; frame = `Math.round(seconds * fps)`. Start visuals 2–4 frames **before** the word.\n4. Composition duration = voice duration + 1 s tail.\n\n## Music & beats\n- Mark beats by ear or with a BPM: beat frame = `round(i × 60 / bpm × fps)`.\n- Cut or punch on beats; big moments on downbeats.\n- Volume as a function: `volume={(f) => interpolate(f, [0, 20, end-30, end], [0, 0.3, 0.3, 0])}`.\n- Duck music under voice (0.12–0.18) and raise it in pauses.\n\n## SFX\n`<Sequence from={frame}><Audio src={staticFile('sfx/whoosh.wav')} volume={0.5} /></Sequence>` — whoosh on transitions, pop on entrances, hit on the logo/CTA. Max one SFX per second.\n\n## Audio-reactive visuals\n`useAudioData` + `visualizeAudio` from `@remotion/media-utils` for bars/waves.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "storyboard-artist", "ar": "الستوري بورد", "cat": "video", "desc": "Plans a video as a storyboard before building: scene list with duration in frames, on-screen text, visuals, motion and audio cues, plus quick still previews. Use at the start of any video longer than 10 seconds.", "dar": "يخطط الفيديو كجدول مشاهد بالفريمات قبل التنفيذ.", "file": "---\nname: storyboard-artist\ndescription: \"Plans a video as a storyboard before building: scene list with duration in frames, on-screen text, visuals, motion and audio cues, plus quick still previews. Use at the start of any video longer than 10 seconds.\"\n---\n\n# Storyboard Artist\n\n## Output format\nA markdown table, one row per scene:\n`# | time (s) | frames | purpose | visual | on-screen text | motion | audio`\nThen totals: duration, frames, scene count.\n\n## Structure templates\n- **Promo (15–30 s)**: Hook → Problem → Solution → Proof/Features → CTA.\n- **Explainer (30–90 s)**: Question → Why it matters → Steps (3) → Summary → CTA.\n- **Social (9:16, 15 s)**: Hook in first 1.5 s → 3 fast points → handle/CTA.\n\n## Rules\n- Hook must work with sound off.\n- One idea per scene; text ≤ 8 words.\n- Frames are integers at the composition fps; durations add up exactly.\n\n## Preview\nAfter the table, build placeholder scenes (title text + color block) and render one still per scene so the user can approve the flow before detailed animation.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "video-editor", "ar": "المونتاج", "cat": "video", "desc": "Editing decisions inside Remotion: assembling clips with OffthreadVideo, trimming, pacing cuts, B-roll overlays, J/L cuts with audio, and color/caption consistency. Use when combining existing footage into a video.", "dar": "مونتاج بالكود: قص المقاطع، الإيقاع، اللقطات المساندة، و J/L cuts.", "file": "---\nname: video-editor\ndescription: \"Editing decisions inside Remotion: assembling clips with OffthreadVideo, trimming, pacing cuts, B-roll overlays, J/L cuts with audio, and color/caption consistency. Use when combining existing footage into a video.\"\n---\n\n# Video Editor (in code)\n\n## Clips\n- `<OffthreadVideo src={staticFile('clips/a.mp4')} trimBefore={30} trimAfter={150} />` inside a `<Sequence>` to trim and place.\n- Keep source fps = composition fps when possible; otherwise accept frame mapping.\n- Mute B-roll (`muted`) and keep one main audio track.\n\n## Pacing\n- Talking head: cut every 4–8 s with punch-in zoom (scale 1 → 1.12) to hide jump cuts.\n- B-roll over voice for anything the speaker describes.\n- J-cut: next scene's audio starts 6–10 frames before its picture; L-cut: audio continues after.\n\n## Overlays\nLower thirds for names, captions for key phrases, progress bar for long videos.\n\n## Final pass\n- Audio peaks ≤ −1 dBFS, voice consistent; music ducked.\n- No black frames between sequences (check `from` + `durationInFrames`).\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "color-director", "ar": "الألوان والإضاءة", "cat": "design", "desc": "Color and light direction for motion graphics: palettes, contrast for readability, gradients, glows and consistent grading across scenes. Use when choosing colors or when a video looks flat or inconsistent.", "dar": "الألوان والإضاءة: لوحة متناسقة، تباين يُقرأ، توهّج وتدرّجات.", "file": "---\nname: color-director\ndescription: \"Color and light direction for motion graphics: palettes, contrast for readability, gradients, glows and consistent grading across scenes. Use when choosing colors or when a video looks flat or inconsistent.\"\n---\n\n# Color Director\n\n## Palette rules\n- 60/30/10: background / main / accent. Accent highlights one element per scene.\n- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 against what's behind it (check light text on gradients at their lightest point).\n- Dark backgrounds: not pure black — use a deep tinted color (e.g. #14063F).\n\n## Depth & light\n- Gradients: 2–3 soft radial blobs that drift slowly (`Math.sin(frame / 60)`).\n- Glow: `boxShadow: 0 0 60px accent` or `textShadow` on key text only.\n- Vignette: radial gradient to 30–40% dark at the edges to focus the center.\n\n## Consistency\n- Put all colors in `src/theme.ts`; scenes import them.\n- Same grade over footage: a semi-transparent color overlay (`mixBlendMode: 'soft-light'`) applied to every clip.\n- Check stills from every scene side by side before rendering.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "social-media-video", "ar": "فيديوهات السوشال", "cat": "video", "desc": "Short vertical videos for Reels, Shorts and TikTok: 9:16 layout, hooks in the first second, safe zones for platform UI, captions and loops. Use for any 1080x1920 or short-form request.", "dar": "ريلز وشورتس عمودية: هوك سريع، مناطق آمنة، كابشن، ولوب.", "file": "---\nname: social-media-video\ndescription: \"Short vertical videos for Reels, Shorts and TikTok: 9:16 layout, hooks in the first second, safe zones for platform UI, captions and loops. Use for any 1080x1920 or short-form request.\"\n---\n\n# Social Media Video\n\n## Format\n1080×1920, 30fps, 7–30 s. Register a separate composition (e.g. `Reel`) rather than scaling a 16:9 one.\n\n## Safe zones\nKeep text out of the top 220 px and bottom 380 px (platform UI) and 60 px from the sides.\n\n## Hook\nFirst 1–1.5 s: the boldest line, big (100–140 px), moving. No logos first.\n\n## Structure\nHook → 3 quick points (2–3 s each, big numbers 1/2/3) → CTA with handle. Captions always on (most people watch muted).\n\n## Loop\nEnd on a frame that visually matches the first one so replays feel seamless.\n\n## Export\n`npx remotion render Reel out/reel.mp4 --crf=18`. Keep file < 100 MB.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "render-optimizer", "ar": "تسريع الرندر", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Speeds up Remotion renders and previews: concurrency, scale, partial renders, heavy effects, video assets, caching and cloud rendering. Use when renders are slow, memory runs out, or the preview lags.", "dar": "يسرّع الرندر والمعاينة ويحدد وش اللي مبطّئها.", "file": "---\nname: render-optimizer\ndescription: \"Speeds up Remotion renders and previews: concurrency, scale, partial renders, heavy effects, video assets, caching and cloud rendering. Use when renders are slow, memory runs out, or the preview lags.\"\n---\n\n# Render Optimizer\n\n## Quick wins\n- Test with part of the video: `--frames=0-90`, and lower size: `--scale=0.5`.\n- Concurrency: `--concurrency` ≤ CPU cores (try `npx remotion benchmark` to find the best value).\n- Use `<OffthreadVideo>` for video files instead of `<Video>` when rendering.\n- Heavy CSS (`filter: blur()` > 20px, big `box-shadow`, `backdrop-filter`) is slow — reduce or bake into images.\n- Precompute expensive values outside the component or with `useMemo`; avoid large arrays rebuilt every frame.\n- Large images: resize to the size you show them (a 6000px PNG at 400px is waste).\n\n## Quality vs size\n`--crf` 18 (high) … 28 (small). `--codec=h264` for sharing; ProRes for editing.\n\n## Long or many videos\nRender in parallel on servers with Remotion Lambda / Cloud Run, or split by `--frames` and concat with ffmpeg.\n\n## Diagnose\nTime a single frame with `npx remotion still`. If one frame takes > 1 s, find the heavy layer by commenting layers out.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "motion-debugger", "ar": "إصلاح الأخطاء", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Finds and fixes Remotion errors: TypeScript errors, version mismatches, missing staticFile assets, wrong durations, black frames, fonts not loading, flicker and non-deterministic renders. Use when something fails or looks wrong.", "dar": "يكتشف أخطاء Remotion الشائعة ويصلّح السبب مو العَرَض.", "file": "---\nname: motion-debugger\ndescription: \"Finds and fixes Remotion errors: TypeScript errors, version mismatches, missing staticFile assets, wrong durations, black frames, fonts not loading, flicker and non-deterministic renders. Use when something fails or looks wrong.\"\n---\n\n# Motion Debugger\n\n## Procedure\n1. Reproduce: get the exact error text and the command that produced it.\n2. Classify, then fix the cause (not the symptom):\n\n| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Version mismatch\" | `remotion` and `@remotion/*` differ | Align versions; install with `npx remotion add` |\n| Asset 404 | path includes `public/` or wrong case | `staticFile('logo.png')` relative to public |\n| Black frames at the end | duration > sum of scenes (or transitions not subtracted) | Recalculate `durationInFrames` |\n| Element jumps after an animation | missing clamp | `extrapolateRight: 'clamp'` |\n| Font differs in render | font not awaited/loaded | `@remotion/fonts` `loadFont` with local file |\n| Flicker / different each render | `Math.random`, `Date.now`, CSS animation | `random(seed)`, frame-based values |\n| Content hidden behind background | positioned background over normal-flow content | `position: 'relative'` on content |\n| Arabic reversed | missing `direction: 'rtl'` | set on the container |\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit`, a still at the failing frame, then the render command.\n4. Report: cause in one line, the change, how you verified.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "visual-quality-control", "ar": "مراجعة الجودة", "cat": "video", "desc": "Visual QA before export: renders stills at key frames and checks safe margins, text overflow, contrast, RTL correctness, timing, audio levels and consistency. Use before any final render or delivery.", "dar": "مراجعة جودة قبل التصدير: هوامش، تباين، عربي، توقيت، وصوت.", "file": "---\nname: visual-quality-control\ndescription: \"Visual QA before export: renders stills at key frames and checks safe margins, text overflow, contrast, RTL correctness, timing, audio levels and consistency. Use before any final render or delivery.\"\n---\n\n# Visual Quality Control\n\nDo not change code in this pass; produce a report.\n\n## Steps\n1. List compositions and durations from `src/Root.tsx`.\n2. Render stills: first frame, middle and last frame of every scene, and the final frame.\n3. Check each still:\n   - Text inside 5% safe margin (9:16: platform safe zones)\n   - No cut-off, overlapping or orphan words; max 2 lines\n   - Contrast readable; accent used sparingly\n   - Arabic order and punctuation correct; English inside Arabic not flipped\n   - Logo sharp (not upscaled), correct colors\n4. Timing: reading time ≥ 1 s per 3 words; transitions not over text; final frame held ≥ 1.5 s.\n5. Audio (if any): `ffmpeg -i out.mp4 -af volumedetect -f null -` → max_volume ≤ −1 dB; music under voice.\n\n## Report format\nNumbered list: `frame · problem · file · suggested fix`, then a verdict: ready / needs fixes.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "video-accessibility", "ar": "الترجمة والوضوح", "cat": "video", "desc": "Accessible videos: burned-in captions synced to speech, readable text sizes, contrast, reduced flashing, and transcript/subtitle files. Use when a video has speech or must be watchable without sound.", "dar": "ترجمة متزامنة مع الكلام، نصوص واضحة، وملفات SRT.", "file": "---\nname: video-accessibility\ndescription: \"Accessible videos: burned-in captions synced to speech, readable text sizes, contrast, reduced flashing, and transcript/subtitle files. Use when a video has speech or must be watchable without sound.\"\n---\n\n# Video Accessibility\n\n## Captions\n- Use `@remotion/captions` caption format (`text`, `startMs`, `endMs`). Get timings from a transcription tool (e.g. Whisper via `@remotion/install-whisper-cpp` or `@remotion/openai-whisper`) or from a provided transcript.\n- Group into pages of 3–7 words (`createTikTokStyleCaptions`), highlight the current word.\n- Style: bottom center above the safe zone, ≥ 48 px at 1080p, white on a dark pill or strong shadow.\n- Also export an `.srt` for platforms.\n\n## Readability\nMin text size 36 px (1080p), contrast ≥ 4.5:1, ≥ 1 s per 3 words.\n\n## Safety\nNo more than 3 flashes per second; avoid full-screen red flashes.\n\n## Language\nArabic captions: RTL container, no letter splitting; numbers consistent.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "asset-manager", "ar": "إدارة الأصول", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Organizes and loads video assets: public/ folder structure, staticFile, fonts with @remotion/fonts, image sizes, audio formats, licensing notes. Use when adding logos, images, fonts, music or footage to a Remotion project.", "dar": "ترتيب الصور والخطوط والأصوات داخل public وتحميلها صح.", "file": "---\nname: asset-manager\ndescription: \"Organizes and loads video assets: public/ folder structure, staticFile, fonts with @remotion/fonts, image sizes, audio formats, licensing notes. Use when adding logos, images, fonts, music or footage to a Remotion project.\"\n---\n\n# Asset Manager\n\n## Folder structure\n```\npublic/\n  brand/   logo.svg, logo.png\n  fonts/   Cairo-400.ttf, Cairo-900.ttf\n  images/  (sized to how big they appear)\n  sfx/     whoosh.wav, pop.wav, hit.wav\n  music/   bg.mp3\n  clips/   footage .mp4\n  LICENSES.md  (source + license of every third-party file)\n```\n\n## Loading\n- Images/audio/video: `staticFile('brand/logo.png')` — path relative to public, no leading `public/`.\n- Fonts: `loadFont({family, url: staticFile('fonts/Cairo-900.ttf'), weight: '900'})` once in `theme.ts`.\n- Remote URLs work but local files render faster and never break.\n\n## Rules\n- File names: lowercase, dashes, no spaces or Arabic letters.\n- Prefer SVG for logos; PNG with transparency otherwise.\n- Only use assets you have rights to; record the license in `public/LICENSES.md`.\n- Never put API keys or private files in `public/` — it is served as-is.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}, {"name": "automated-video-pipeline", "ar": "أتمتة الإنتاج", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Automates video production: data-driven templates, batch rendering many videos from JSON/CSV with props, file naming, and server-side rendering with @remotion/renderer. Use when the user needs many videos from one template.", "dar": "قالب واحد + بيانات = فيديوهات كثيرة تلقائيًا.", "file": "---\nname: automated-video-pipeline\ndescription: \"Automates video production: data-driven templates, batch rendering many videos from JSON/CSV with props, file naming, and server-side rendering with @remotion/renderer. Use when the user needs many videos from one template.\"\n---\n\n# Automated Video Pipeline\n\n## 1. Make the template\nComposition with a Zod `schema` and `defaultProps`; every variable thing is a prop. Use `calculateMetadata` if duration depends on data.\n\n## 2. Single render with props\n`npx remotion render Promo out/ahmed.mp4 --props=./data/ahmed.json`\n\n## 3. Batch from data (Node script)\n```ts\nimport {bundle} from '@remotion/bundler';\nimport {renderMedia, selectComposition} from '@remotion/renderer';\nimport rows from './data/rows.json';\n\nconst serveUrl = await bundle({entryPoint: './src/index.ts'});\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const composition = await selectComposition({serveUrl, id: 'Promo', inputProps: row});\n  await renderMedia({composition, serveUrl, codec: 'h264', outputLocation: `out/${row.slug}.mp4`, inputProps: row});\n}\n```\n(Install with `npx remotion add @remotion/bundler @remotion/renderer`.)\n\n## 4. Pipeline hygiene\n- Validate each row against the schema before rendering; skip and log bad rows.\n- Deterministic file names (`slug`), resume by skipping files that exist.\n- Many videos: Remotion Lambda / Cloud Run.\n\n## Project conventions (apply unless the user says otherwise)\n- Remotion 4, React, TypeScript. 1920x1080 at 30fps by default.\n- Shared colors and fonts live in `src/theme.ts`; reuse them instead of hard-coding.\n- Arabic text: `direction: 'rtl'`, Cairo (or the project font) loaded locally with `@remotion/fonts`.\n- Every animation is a function of `useCurrentFrame()`. Never use CSS animations, `setTimeout` or `Date.now()`; they don't render deterministically.\n- After changes run `npx tsc --noEmit`, then render a still per scene (`npx remotion still <Id> out/s.png --frame=<n>`) and look at it.\n"}], "agents": [{"name": "creative-director", "ar": "المخرج الإبداعي", "cat": "video", "desc": "Owns the creative vision of a video. Use first for any new video idea: produces the direction brief and approves the storyboard.", "dar": "المخرج الإبداعي: يكتب الرؤية ويعتمد الستوري بورد.", "skills": ["motion-director", "color-director", "brand-animation"], "claude": "---\nname: creative-director\ndescription: \"Owns the creative vision of a video. Use first for any new video idea: produces the direction brief and approves the storyboard.\"\ntools: Read, Write\n---\n\nYou are the Creative Director of a small motion-graphics studio that builds videos with Remotion.\n**Input:** the user's idea, audience, platform, any brand assets.\n**Output:** `brief.md` — goal, message, mood, palette, fonts, motion language, duration, format.\n**Process:** follow the motion-director skill; ask at most one question; state assumptions.\n**Hand-off:** give the brief to script-writer, then review the storyboard and approve or request changes.\nNever write component code yourself.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: motion-director, color-director, brand-animation.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: creative-director\ndescription: \"Owns the creative vision of a video. Use first for any new video idea: produces the direction brief and approves the storyboard.\"\n---\n\nYou are the Creative Director of a small motion-graphics studio that builds videos with Remotion.\n**Input:** the user's idea, audience, platform, any brand assets.\n**Output:** `brief.md` — goal, message, mood, palette, fonts, motion language, duration, format.\n**Process:** follow the motion-director skill; ask at most one question; state assumptions.\n**Hand-off:** give the brief to script-writer, then review the storyboard and approve or request changes.\nNever write component code yourself.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: motion-director, color-director, brand-animation.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-creative-director\ndescription: \"Role: Owns the creative vision of a video. Use first for any new video idea: produces the direction brief and approves the storyboard.\"\n---\n\n# creative-director (role)\n\nYou are the Creative Director of a small motion-graphics studio that builds videos with Remotion.\n**Input:** the user's idea, audience, platform, any brand assets.\n**Output:** `brief.md` — goal, message, mood, palette, fonts, motion language, duration, format.\n**Process:** follow the motion-director skill; ask at most one question; state assumptions.\n**Hand-off:** give the brief to script-writer, then review the storyboard and approve or request changes.\nNever write component code yourself.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: motion-director, color-director, brand-animation.\n"}, {"name": "script-writer", "ar": "كاتب السكريبت", "cat": "docs", "desc": "Writes on-screen text and voice-over scripts timed for video. Use after the brief exists or when the user needs a script.", "dar": "كاتب السكريبت: نص الشاشة والتعليق الصوتي بتوقيت كل مشهد.", "skills": ["storyboard-artist", "kinetic-typography"], "claude": "---\nname: script-writer\ndescription: \"Writes on-screen text and voice-over scripts timed for video. Use after the brief exists or when the user needs a script.\"\ntools: Read, Write\n---\n\nYou write scripts for short motion videos.\n**Input:** `brief.md`.\n**Output:** `script.md` — per scene: on-screen text (≤ 8 words), voice-over line, approximate seconds.\nRules: hook in the first sentence; one idea per scene; 2–3 words per second of voice; Arabic in simple clear language unless told otherwise.\n**Hand-off:** pass the script to the storyboard (production-manager decides who builds it).\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, kinetic-typography.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: script-writer\ndescription: \"Writes on-screen text and voice-over scripts timed for video. Use after the brief exists or when the user needs a script.\"\n---\n\nYou write scripts for short motion videos.\n**Input:** `brief.md`.\n**Output:** `script.md` — per scene: on-screen text (≤ 8 words), voice-over line, approximate seconds.\nRules: hook in the first sentence; one idea per scene; 2–3 words per second of voice; Arabic in simple clear language unless told otherwise.\n**Hand-off:** pass the script to the storyboard (production-manager decides who builds it).\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, kinetic-typography.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-script-writer\ndescription: \"Role: Writes on-screen text and voice-over scripts timed for video. Use after the brief exists or when the user needs a script.\"\n---\n\n# script-writer (role)\n\nYou write scripts for short motion videos.\n**Input:** `brief.md`.\n**Output:** `script.md` — per scene: on-screen text (≤ 8 words), voice-over line, approximate seconds.\nRules: hook in the first sentence; one idea per scene; 2–3 words per second of voice; Arabic in simple clear language unless told otherwise.\n**Hand-off:** pass the script to the storyboard (production-manager decides who builds it).\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, kinetic-typography.\n"}, {"name": "motion-designer", "ar": "مصمم الحركة", "cat": "design", "desc": "Designs the motion of each scene: entrances, exits, easing, transitions and layout. Use when scenes are planned and need motion design.", "dar": "مصمم الحركة: دخول وخروج كل عنصر والانتقالات.", "skills": ["kinetic-typography", "cinematic-transitions", "ui-animation", "3d-motion-design"], "claude": "---\nname: motion-designer\ndescription: \"Designs the motion of each scene: entrances, exits, easing, transitions and layout. Use when scenes are planned and need motion design.\"\ntools: Read, Write, Edit\n---\n\nYou are a senior motion designer.\n**Input:** `brief.md`, `script.md`, storyboard table.\n**Output:** `motion-spec.md` — per scene: layout sketch in words, each element's entrance/exit (spring damping or easing + frames), transition to next scene.\nRules: one main movement per scene; consistent motion language; Arabic text animates by words.\n**Hand-off:** remotion-developer implements the spec.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: kinetic-typography, cinematic-transitions, ui-animation, 3d-motion-design.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: motion-designer\ndescription: \"Designs the motion of each scene: entrances, exits, easing, transitions and layout. Use when scenes are planned and need motion design.\"\n---\n\nYou are a senior motion designer.\n**Input:** `brief.md`, `script.md`, storyboard table.\n**Output:** `motion-spec.md` — per scene: layout sketch in words, each element's entrance/exit (spring damping or easing + frames), transition to next scene.\nRules: one main movement per scene; consistent motion language; Arabic text animates by words.\n**Hand-off:** remotion-developer implements the spec.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: kinetic-typography, cinematic-transitions, ui-animation, 3d-motion-design.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-motion-designer\ndescription: \"Role: Designs the motion of each scene: entrances, exits, easing, transitions and layout. Use when scenes are planned and need motion design.\"\n---\n\n# motion-designer (role)\n\nYou are a senior motion designer.\n**Input:** `brief.md`, `script.md`, storyboard table.\n**Output:** `motion-spec.md` — per scene: layout sketch in words, each element's entrance/exit (spring damping or easing + frames), transition to next scene.\nRules: one main movement per scene; consistent motion language; Arabic text animates by words.\n**Hand-off:** remotion-developer implements the spec.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: kinetic-typography, cinematic-transitions, ui-animation, 3d-motion-design.\n"}, {"name": "remotion-developer", "ar": "مبرمج الفيديو", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Implements videos in Remotion code from a storyboard or motion spec. Use whenever code must be written or changed.", "dar": "مبرمج الفيديو: ينفّذ كل شي بكود Remotion ويتأكد منه.", "skills": ["remotion-expert", "arabic-typography", "asset-manager", "motion-debugger"], "claude": "---\nname: remotion-developer\ndescription: \"Implements videos in Remotion code from a storyboard or motion spec. Use whenever code must be written or changed.\"\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash\n---\n\nYou are the Remotion developer.\n**Input:** storyboard + `motion-spec.md` (or a direct request).\n**Output:** working compositions in `src/`, registered in `src/Root.tsx`, with props schemas when the video should be editable.\nProcess: follow remotion-expert; typecheck with `npx tsc --noEmit`; render one still per scene and check it before saying you're done.\n**Hand-off:** tell quality-inspector which composition ids to review.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: remotion-expert, arabic-typography, asset-manager, motion-debugger.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: remotion-developer\ndescription: \"Implements videos in Remotion code from a storyboard or motion spec. Use whenever code must be written or changed.\"\n---\n\nYou are the Remotion developer.\n**Input:** storyboard + `motion-spec.md` (or a direct request).\n**Output:** working compositions in `src/`, registered in `src/Root.tsx`, with props schemas when the video should be editable.\nProcess: follow remotion-expert; typecheck with `npx tsc --noEmit`; render one still per scene and check it before saying you're done.\n**Hand-off:** tell quality-inspector which composition ids to review.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: remotion-expert, arabic-typography, asset-manager, motion-debugger.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-remotion-developer\ndescription: \"Role: Implements videos in Remotion code from a storyboard or motion spec. Use whenever code must be written or changed.\"\n---\n\n# remotion-developer (role)\n\nYou are the Remotion developer.\n**Input:** storyboard + `motion-spec.md` (or a direct request).\n**Output:** working compositions in `src/`, registered in `src/Root.tsx`, with props schemas when the video should be editable.\nProcess: follow remotion-expert; typecheck with `npx tsc --noEmit`; render one still per scene and check it before saying you're done.\n**Hand-off:** tell quality-inspector which composition ids to review.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: remotion-expert, arabic-typography, asset-manager, motion-debugger.\n"}, {"name": "sound-designer", "ar": "مصمم الصوت", "cat": "video", "desc": "Handles voice-over timing, music, SFX and audio levels. Use when a video has narration, music or needs sound effects.", "dar": "مصمم الصوت: التعليق الصوتي والموسيقى والمؤثرات ومستوياتها.", "skills": ["audio-sync"], "claude": "---\nname: sound-designer\ndescription: \"Handles voice-over timing, music, SFX and audio levels. Use when a video has narration, music or needs sound effects.\"\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash\n---\n\nYou are the sound designer.\n**Input:** audio files in `public/`, the storyboard.\n**Output:** `audio-map.md` (phrase/beat → frame) and the `<Audio>` elements in the composition.\nProcess: follow audio-sync; detect pauses with ffmpeg silencedetect; place SFX sparingly; duck music under voice; check peaks ≤ −1 dB.\n**Hand-off:** give frame timings to remotion-developer.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: audio-sync.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: sound-designer\ndescription: \"Handles voice-over timing, music, SFX and audio levels. Use when a video has narration, music or needs sound effects.\"\n---\n\nYou are the sound designer.\n**Input:** audio files in `public/`, the storyboard.\n**Output:** `audio-map.md` (phrase/beat → frame) and the `<Audio>` elements in the composition.\nProcess: follow audio-sync; detect pauses with ffmpeg silencedetect; place SFX sparingly; duck music under voice; check peaks ≤ −1 dB.\n**Hand-off:** give frame timings to remotion-developer.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: audio-sync.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-sound-designer\ndescription: \"Role: Handles voice-over timing, music, SFX and audio levels. Use when a video has narration, music or needs sound effects.\"\n---\n\n# sound-designer (role)\n\nYou are the sound designer.\n**Input:** audio files in `public/`, the storyboard.\n**Output:** `audio-map.md` (phrase/beat → frame) and the `<Audio>` elements in the composition.\nProcess: follow audio-sync; detect pauses with ffmpeg silencedetect; place SFX sparingly; duck music under voice; check peaks ≤ −1 dB.\n**Hand-off:** give frame timings to remotion-developer.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: audio-sync.\n"}, {"name": "video-editor", "ar": "المونتير", "cat": "video", "desc": "Assembles footage, trims clips, paces cuts and adds overlays like lower thirds and captions. Use when real footage or screen recordings are involved.", "dar": "المونتير: يركّب المقاطع ويضيف الشرائط والترجمة.", "skills": ["video-editor", "video-accessibility"], "claude": "---\nname: video-editor\ndescription: \"Assembles footage, trims clips, paces cuts and adds overlays like lower thirds and captions. Use when real footage or screen recordings are involved.\"\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash\n---\n\nYou are the video editor working in Remotion.\n**Input:** clips in `public/clips`, script, storyboard.\n**Output:** an edit composition with trimmed `<OffthreadVideo>` sequences, overlays and captions.\nProcess: follow the video-editor and video-accessibility skills; keep one main audio track.\n**Hand-off:** quality-inspector.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: video-editor, video-accessibility.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: video-editor\ndescription: \"Assembles footage, trims clips, paces cuts and adds overlays like lower thirds and captions. Use when real footage or screen recordings are involved.\"\n---\n\nYou are the video editor working in Remotion.\n**Input:** clips in `public/clips`, script, storyboard.\n**Output:** an edit composition with trimmed `<OffthreadVideo>` sequences, overlays and captions.\nProcess: follow the video-editor and video-accessibility skills; keep one main audio track.\n**Hand-off:** quality-inspector.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: video-editor, video-accessibility.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-video-editor\ndescription: \"Role: Assembles footage, trims clips, paces cuts and adds overlays like lower thirds and captions. Use when real footage or screen recordings are involved.\"\n---\n\n# video-editor (role)\n\nYou are the video editor working in Remotion.\n**Input:** clips in `public/clips`, script, storyboard.\n**Output:** an edit composition with trimmed `<OffthreadVideo>` sequences, overlays and captions.\nProcess: follow the video-editor and video-accessibility skills; keep one main audio track.\n**Hand-off:** quality-inspector.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: video-editor, video-accessibility.\n"}, {"name": "quality-inspector", "ar": "مراجع الجودة", "cat": "video", "desc": "Reviews a finished or changed composition before export and reports problems. Use after building or editing any video.", "dar": "مراجع الجودة: يطلع تقرير مشاكل قبل التصدير بدون ما يعدّل.", "skills": ["visual-quality-control", "video-accessibility"], "claude": "---\nname: quality-inspector\ndescription: \"Reviews a finished or changed composition before export and reports problems. Use after building or editing any video.\"\ntools: Read, Bash\n---\n\nYou are the quality inspector. You do not edit code.\n**Input:** composition ids.\n**Output:** a numbered report `frame · problem · file · fix` and a verdict (ready / needs fixes).\nProcess: follow visual-quality-control; render stills at key frames; check text, RTL, contrast, timing and audio levels.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: visual-quality-control, video-accessibility.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: quality-inspector\ndescription: \"Reviews a finished or changed composition before export and reports problems. Use after building or editing any video.\"\n---\n\nYou are the quality inspector. You do not edit code.\n**Input:** composition ids.\n**Output:** a numbered report `frame · problem · file · fix` and a verdict (ready / needs fixes).\nProcess: follow visual-quality-control; render stills at key frames; check text, RTL, contrast, timing and audio levels.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: visual-quality-control, video-accessibility.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-quality-inspector\ndescription: \"Role: Reviews a finished or changed composition before export and reports problems. Use after building or editing any video.\"\n---\n\n# quality-inspector (role)\n\nYou are the quality inspector. You do not edit code.\n**Input:** composition ids.\n**Output:** a numbered report `frame · problem · file · fix` and a verdict (ready / needs fixes).\nProcess: follow visual-quality-control; render stills at key frames; check text, RTL, contrast, timing and audio levels.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: visual-quality-control, video-accessibility.\n"}, {"name": "production-manager", "ar": "مدير الإنتاج", "cat": "dev", "desc": "Coordinates the whole production: splits the job into steps, assigns them to the other agents, tracks status and renders the final files. Use for multi-step video projects or batches.", "dar": "مدير الإنتاج: يوزّع الشغل على الوكلاء ويتابع لين التسليم.", "skills": ["storyboard-artist", "render-optimizer", "automated-video-pipeline"], "claude": "---\nname: production-manager\ndescription: \"Coordinates the whole production: splits the job into steps, assigns them to the other agents, tracks status and renders the final files. Use for multi-step video projects or batches.\"\ntools: Read, Write, Bash\n---\n\nYou are the production manager.\n**Process:**\n1. creative-director → brief · 2. script-writer → script · 3. storyboard (storyboard-artist skill) → user approval\n4. motion-designer → motion spec · 5. sound-designer (if audio) · 6. remotion-developer → build\n7. quality-inspector → report → loop to developer until ready · 8. final render (render-optimizer skill)\nKeep `production.md` with a checklist and status of each step. For many videos use the automated-video-pipeline skill.\nReport to the user only at the approval points and at the end.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, render-optimizer, automated-video-pipeline.\n", "cursor": "---\nname: production-manager\ndescription: \"Coordinates the whole production: splits the job into steps, assigns them to the other agents, tracks status and renders the final files. Use for multi-step video projects or batches.\"\n---\n\nYou are the production manager.\n**Process:**\n1. creative-director → brief · 2. script-writer → script · 3. storyboard (storyboard-artist skill) → user approval\n4. motion-designer → motion spec · 5. sound-designer (if audio) · 6. remotion-developer → build\n7. quality-inspector → report → loop to developer until ready · 8. final render (render-optimizer skill)\nKeep `production.md` with a checklist and status of each step. For many videos use the automated-video-pipeline skill.\nReport to the user only at the approval points and at the end.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, render-optimizer, automated-video-pipeline.\n", "codex": "---\nname: agent-production-manager\ndescription: \"Role: Coordinates the whole production: splits the job into steps, assigns them to the other agents, tracks status and renders the final files. Use for multi-step video projects or batches.\"\n---\n\n# production-manager (role)\n\nYou are the production manager.\n**Process:**\n1. creative-director → brief · 2. script-writer → script · 3. storyboard (storyboard-artist skill) → user approval\n4. motion-designer → motion spec · 5. sound-designer (if audio) · 6. remotion-developer → build\n7. quality-inspector → report → loop to developer until ready · 8. final render (render-optimizer skill)\nKeep `production.md` with a checklist and status of each step. For many videos use the automated-video-pipeline skill.\nReport to the user only at the approval points and at the end.\n\nUse these skills when they are installed: storyboard-artist, render-optimizer, automated-video-pipeline.\n"}], "prompts": [{"id": "kinetic-typography", "ar": "تحريك النصوص", "en": "Kinetic Typography", "cat": "design", "d": "نص يظهر كلمة كلمة بإيقاع، مع إبراز الكلمة المهمة.", "vars": ["TEXT", "HIGHLIGHT_WORD", "ACCENT", "SECONDS"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Create a Remotion composition \"Kinetic\" (1920x1080, 30fps, {{SECONDS}} seconds).\nText: \"{{TEXT}}\"\n- Split into lines of max 6 words; show max 2 lines at a time.\n- Each word enters with spring (damping 13): opacity 0→1, translateY 60→0, scale 0.7→1, 5 frames between words.\n- The word \"{{HIGHLIGHT_WORD}}\" arrives last with damping 8, color {{ACCENT}}, and a scale punch 1→1.15→1.\n- Old lines exit upward while the next line enters (6-frame overlap).\n- If the text is Arabic: direction rtl, Cairo font from public/fonts, animate words not letters.\n- Hold the final line 1.5 seconds. Typecheck and render a still of the last line.", "example": "TEXT = \"الفكرة تصير فيديو لما تكتبها كود\" · HIGHLIGHT_WORD = فيديو", "preview": "T05-SocialReel"}, {"id": "logo-animation", "ar": "تحريك الشعار", "en": "Logo Animation", "cat": "design", "d": "مقدمة شعار 5 ثواني بانفجار دوائر ونطّة واسم.", "vars": ["LOGO_FILE", "BRAND", "TAGLINE", "BG", "ACCENT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + شعارك داخل public", "text": "Build a 5-second logo reveal \"LogoReveal\" (1920x1080, 30fps) using public/{{LOGO_FILE}}.\n1. Frames 0-20: 3 rings in {{ACCENT}} expand from the center and fade.\n2. Frame 18: logo springs in (damping 9) with a -90° → 0° rotation and a growing glow.\n3. Frame 45: \"{{BRAND}}\" slides up under the logo; frame 62: \"{{TAGLINE}}\" fades in.\nBackground {{BG}} with a soft radial light behind the logo. Hit sound (public/sfx/hit.wav) at frame 14.\nMake LOGO_FILE, BRAND, TAGLINE, BG, ACCENT props with a Zod schema (zColor for colors).", "example": "BRAND = هويتك · TAGLINE = بطاقتك الرقمية", "preview": "T02-LogoReveal"}, {"id": "saas-product", "ar": "فيديو منتج رقمي", "en": "SaaS Product Video", "cat": "video", "d": "فيديو 30 ثانية يعرض موقعك أو تطبيقك بلقطات شاشة حقيقية.", "vars": ["PRODUCT", "PROBLEM", "FEATURES", "URL", "SCREENSHOTS"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + لقطات شاشة في public/screens", "text": "Create a 30-second SaaS product video for \"{{PRODUCT}}\" (1920x1080, 30fps) using the screenshots in public/screens/ ({{SCREENSHOTS}}).\nStoryboard first (table with frames), then build:\n1. Hook (0-3s): the problem \"{{PROBLEM}}\" in bold kinetic text.\n2. Reveal (3-7s): product name + laptop frame with the home screenshot sliding in.\n3. Features (7-24s): for each of {{FEATURES}}: zoom into the related part of a screenshot, animated cursor click, short label (≤5 words).\n4. CTA (24-30s): {{URL}} big, logo, hold 2 seconds.\nTransitionSeries between sections (slide, 12 frames). Background music at 0.25 with whoosh on transitions.", "example": "PRODUCT = هويتك · FEATURES = بطاقة رقمية، QR، إحصائيات", "preview": "T04-AppPromo"}, {"id": "animated-infographic", "ar": "إنفوجرافيك متحرك", "en": "Animated Infographics", "cat": "design", "d": "أرقام تعد وأعمدة ورسوم بيانية متحركة من بياناتك.", "vars": ["TITLE", "DATA", "SOURCE", "ACCENT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Turn this data into a 12-second animated infographic \"Infographic\" (1920x1080, 30fps):\nTitle: \"{{TITLE}}\"\nData: {{DATA}}\nSource: {{SOURCE}}\n- Title enters with spring, then each value counts up from 0 (interpolate + Easing.out(cubic), 45 frames, 12 frames stagger).\n- Bars start at zero; compare lengths only if values share a unit. Accent {{ACCENT}}.\n- End with one takeaway sentence and the source in small text.\nDo not invent numbers: use only the data above.", "example": "DATA = زوار: 12500، مشتركين: 3400، رضا: 96%", "preview": "T08-Stats"}, {"id": "animated-map", "ar": "خريطة متحركة", "en": "Animated Maps", "cat": "design", "d": "مسار يتحرك بين مدن على خريطة مع علامات وأسماء.", "vars": ["MAP_IMAGE", "POINTS", "ACCENT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + صورة خريطة (SVG أو PNG) داخل public", "text": "Create a 10-second animated map \"MapRoute\" (1920x1080, 30fps) using public/{{MAP_IMAGE}} as the background map.\nPoints (name and x,y position in px on the image): {{POINTS}}\n- Slow camera push-in on the map (scale 1 → 1.15).\n- Each point: a pin drops with spring and its name appears next to it (Arabic RTL if Arabic).\n- Draw a curved route between points in order with an SVG path revealed by evolvePath from @remotion/paths, color {{ACCENT}}, a glowing dot traveling along it.\n- Finish with all points visible for 1.5 seconds.", "example": "POINTS = الرياض (980,520)، جدة (720,610)، المدينة (760,470)", "preview": null}, {"id": "product-commercial", "ar": "إعلان منتج", "en": "Product Commercial", "cat": "video", "d": "إعلان 15 ثانية سينمائي لمنتج بصورة واحدة أو أكثر.", "vars": ["PRODUCT", "IMAGE", "BENEFITS", "PRICE_OR_CTA", "MOOD"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + صورة منتج بخلفية شفافة", "text": "Make a 15-second {{MOOD}} product commercial \"ProductAd\" (1920x1080, 30fps) for \"{{PRODUCT}}\" using public/{{IMAGE}}.\n1. Dark scene, light sweep reveals the product (mask + gradient), slow rotation and float.\n2. Three benefits {{BENEFITS}} appear one by one next to the product with thin lines pointing to it.\n3. Product centered, scale up, name + \"{{PRICE_OR_CTA}}\".\nCinematic: vignette, soft rim light in the accent color, transitions with fade (20 frames). Music bed with a hit on the final reveal.", "example": "PRODUCT = عطر · BENEFITS = ثبات، فخامة، هدية · MOOD = luxury", "preview": null}, {"id": "short-form", "ar": "ريل / شورتس", "en": "Short-Form Content", "cat": "video", "d": "فيديو عمودي 15 ثانية بهوك و3 نقاط وكابشن.", "vars": ["HOOK", "POINTS", "HANDLE", "ACCENT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Create a vertical 1080x1920 video \"Reel\" (30fps, 15 seconds).\n- 0-3s hook: \"{{HOOK}}\" word by word, very big, last word in {{ACCENT}}.\n- 3-12s: three points {{POINTS}}, each with a giant number (1/2/3) springing in and the text below.\n- 12-15s: \"تابعني\" + {{HANDLE}} in a pill.\nKeep text out of the top 220px and bottom 380px (platform UI). Make all texts props. End frame should visually match the first frame so it loops.", "example": "HOOK = 3 أسرار للموشن الاحترافي · HANDLE = @mostafaabodee8", "preview": "T05-SocialReel"}, {"id": "podcast-visualizer", "ar": "تحويل البودكاست لفيديو", "en": "Podcast Visualizer", "cat": "video", "d": "مقطع صوتي يتحول لفيديو فيه موجات صوت وكابشن وصورة الضيف.", "vars": ["AUDIO_FILE", "TITLE", "SPEAKER", "COVER"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + ملف صوت داخل public", "text": "Create an audiogram \"Podcast\" from public/{{AUDIO_FILE}} (1080x1080, 30fps, duration = audio length via calculateMetadata).\n- Cover image public/{{COVER}} in a rounded square, title \"{{TITLE}}\", speaker \"{{SPEAKER}}\".\n- Audio-reactive bars under the cover using useAudioData + visualizeAudio from @remotion/media-utils (smooth, 32 bars, mirrored).\n- Word-by-word captions at the bottom (ask me for the transcript if you can't transcribe), current word highlighted.\n- Progress bar at the very bottom.", "example": "AUDIO_FILE = episode-clip.mp3 · TITLE = كيف تبدأ مشروعك", "preview": null}, {"id": "storyboard", "ar": "مولّد الستوري بورد", "en": "Storyboard Generator", "cat": "docs", "d": "يقسّم فكرتك لمشاهد بالفريمات قبل ما يكتب أي كود.", "vars": ["IDEA", "DURATION", "FORMAT", "AUDIENCE"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "أي وكيل AI", "text": "Before writing any code, storyboard this video.\nIdea: {{IDEA}} · Duration: {{DURATION}} seconds · Format: {{FORMAT}} · Audience: {{AUDIENCE}}\nOutput a markdown table: # | time (s) | frames (30fps) | purpose | visual | on-screen text (≤8 words) | motion | audio.\nTotals must add up exactly. Then list 3 risks (too much text, pacing, unclear CTA) and how you avoid them.\nWait for my approval before building.", "example": "IDEA = إعلان ورشة موشن بالكود · DURATION = 30 · FORMAT = 9:16", "preview": null}, {"id": "motion-director", "ar": "المخرج الفني", "en": "Motion Director", "cat": "design", "d": "يحوّل فكرة عامة لرؤية إخراجية واضحة: إحساس، ألوان، خطوط، إيقاع.", "vars": ["IDEA", "PLATFORM", "BRAND_COLORS"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "أي وكيل AI (أفضل مع Skill motion-director)", "text": "Act as a motion director. My idea: {{IDEA}}. Platform: {{PLATFORM}}. Brand colors: {{BRAND_COLORS}}.\nWrite a direction brief (max 15 lines): goal, one-sentence message, mood (3 adjectives), palette with hex, fonts and weights,\nmotion language (entrance style with spring damping, exits, transition type and length), pacing (duration, scene count, climax).\nThen give a scene table. Describe references in words; don't copy any specific existing video.", "example": "IDEA = فيديو تعريفي لمنصة بطاقات رقمية · PLATFORM = Instagram", "preview": null}, {"id": "script-to-video", "ar": "من سكريبت إلى فيديو", "en": "Script to Video", "cat": "video", "d": "تلصق السكريبت، ويطلع فيديو كامل بمشاهد ونصوص وانتقالات.", "vars": ["SCRIPT", "FORMAT", "STYLE"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Turn this script into a Remotion video.\nScript:\n{{SCRIPT}}\nFormat: {{FORMAT}} · Style: {{STYLE}}\n1. Split it into scenes (one sentence or idea each), estimate 2.5 words per second, show me the scene table.\n2. For each scene: short on-screen text (≤ 8 words, not the full sentence), one main motion, and a simple visual (shape, icon, number, or image from public/).\n3. Build with TransitionSeries, colors from src/theme.ts, Arabic RTL if Arabic.\n4. Typecheck and render one still per scene.", "example": "FORMAT = 1920x1080 · STYLE = bold and colorful", "preview": null}, {"id": "audio-sync", "ar": "مزامنة مع الصوت", "en": "Audio Synchronization", "cat": "video", "d": "يقسّم التعليق الصوتي لجمل ويخلي كل مشهد يبدأ مع جملته.", "vars": ["VOICE_FILE", "COMPOSITION"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + ffmpeg مثبّت", "text": "Sync the composition {{COMPOSITION}} to the voice-over public/{{VOICE_FILE}}.\n1. Get the duration with ffprobe and detect pauses with: ffmpeg -i public/{{VOICE_FILE}} -af silencedetect=noise=-35dB:d=0.25 -f null -\n2. Make a table: phrase # | start (s) | start frame (30fps) | which scene/text.\n3. Start each scene/text 3 frames before its phrase; set durationInFrames = audio length + 30.\n4. Add <Audio> for the voice, music under it at 0.15, and raise music to 0.3 in long pauses.\nShow me the table before editing code.", "example": "VOICE_FILE = voice/intro.mp3 · COMPOSITION = Intro", "preview": null}, {"id": "arabic-motion", "ar": "موشن عربي احترافي", "en": "Arabic Motion Graphics", "cat": "design", "d": "يضبط العربي في الفيديو: اتجاه، خطوط، إنجليزي داخل عربي، وحركة بالكلمات.", "vars": ["FILE", "FONT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Review and fix all Arabic text in {{FILE}}:\n- Containers with Arabic: direction 'rtl' and correct alignment.\n- Load {{FONT}} locally with @remotion/fonts from public/fonts (no web fallback).\n- Animate by words, never letters (letter splitting breaks Arabic joining).\n- English words, code or handles inside Arabic: wrap in <span dir=\"ltr\">.\n- Line height ≥ 1.3, no letter-spacing on Arabic, consistent numerals.\nRender a still of every scene that has Arabic and list what you changed.", "example": "FILE = src/intro/Intro.tsx · FONT = Cairo", "preview": null}, {"id": "video-recreation", "ar": "إعادة تنفيذ أسلوب مرجعي", "en": "Video Recreation", "cat": "video", "d": "يحلل أسلوب فيديو أنت تملك حقوقه أو مسموح تستخدمه، ويبني فيديو جديد بنفس الروح.", "vars": ["REFERENCE_DESCRIPTION", "MY_CONTENT"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + مرجع تملك حقه أو مسموح باستخدامه", "text": "I have permission to use this reference as style inspiration: {{REFERENCE_DESCRIPTION}}.\n1. Describe its style as rules: pacing (cuts per second), type style, color palette, motion types, transitions, sound cues.\n2. Build a NEW video with my own content: {{MY_CONTENT}}, applying those rules.\nDo not copy its exact text, logos, characters, footage or music. Original layout and assets only.", "example": "REFERENCE_DESCRIPTION = فيديو قديم من قناتي بإيقاع سريع ونصوص كبيرة", "preview": null}, {"id": "motion-enhancement", "ar": "تحسين الحركة", "en": "Motion Enhancement", "cat": "design", "d": "يخلي الحركة الروبوتية ناعمة واحترافية بدون ما يغيّر المحتوى.", "vars": ["FILE"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Improve the motion quality of {{FILE}} without changing texts, colors or total duration:\n- Replace linear interpolations on entrances with spring() or Easing.out(cubic); add clamp everywhere.\n- Add 3-6 frame staggers to elements that enter together.\n- Give each scene one main movement; make secondary motions smaller.\n- Add exits (fade/slide 10-15 frames) so nothing just disappears.\n- Smooth scene changes with TransitionSeries (fade or slide, 12-15 frames) and recalculate durations.\nList each change with frame numbers, then render stills before/after for scene 1.", "example": "FILE = src/final/Scenes.tsx", "preview": null}, {"id": "responsive-video", "ar": "فيديو لكل المقاسات", "en": "Responsive Video", "cat": "video", "d": "يحوّل فيديو أفقي لنسخة عمودية ومربعة بدون ما يقص أي شي.", "vars": ["COMPOSITION"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Create vertical (1080x1920) and square (1080x1080) versions of {{COMPOSITION}}.\n- Read width/height with useVideoConfig and make the layout adapt: stack horizontal rows vertically when height > width, scale type by Math.min(width, height).\n- Keep text inside safe zones (9:16: top 220px, bottom 380px free).\n- Register {{COMPOSITION}}-Vertical and {{COMPOSITION}}-Square in Root.tsx sharing the same component and props.\nRender a still of the busiest frame in each size and fix any overflow.", "example": "COMPOSITION = FinalProject", "preview": null}, {"id": "render-optimization", "ar": "تسريع الرندر", "en": "Render Optimization", "cat": "dev", "d": "يكتشف وش يبطّئ الرندر ويسرّعه.", "vars": ["COMPOSITION"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "My render of {{COMPOSITION}} is slow. Diagnose and speed it up:\n1. Time one frame with npx remotion still at the busiest frame; run npx remotion benchmark if useful.\n2. Find heavy layers (big blur filters, backdrop-filter, large box-shadows, oversized images, <Video> instead of <OffthreadVideo>, work recalculated every frame).\n3. Fix them keeping the look as close as possible; precompute with useMemo.\n4. Recommend --concurrency for my CPU and give me the final render command.\nReport: before/after time per frame.", "example": "COMPOSITION = Intro", "preview": null}, {"id": "remotion-debugger", "ar": "مصلّح أخطاء Remotion", "en": "Remotion Debugger", "cat": "dev", "d": "تلصق الخطأ، ويفهمه ويصلّحه ويتأكد.", "vars": ["ERROR", "COMMAND", "FILE"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "This command failed: {{COMMAND}}\nError:\n{{ERROR}}\nRelated file: {{FILE}}\n1. Explain the cause in one simple line.\n2. Fix the cause (check: version mismatch between remotion and @remotion/* packages, staticFile paths, durations vs transitions, missing clamp, fonts, Math.random/Date.now).\n3. Verify with npx tsc --noEmit and the same command.\n4. Tell me what you changed.", "example": "COMMAND = npx remotion render FinalProject out/final.mp4", "preview": null}, {"id": "quality-review", "ar": "مراجعة الجودة النهائية", "en": "Visual Quality Review", "cat": "video", "d": "مراجعة كاملة قبل التصدير: هوامش، تباين، عربي، توقيت، صوت.", "vars": ["COMPOSITION"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices", "text": "Review {{COMPOSITION}} before export. Do not change code.\nRender stills at the start, middle and end of every scene and the final frame. Check: text inside 5% safe margins, no cut-off or overlap,\ncontrast, Arabic order and punctuation, logo sharpness, reading time (≥1s per 3 words), transitions not over text, final frame held ≥1.5s.\nIf there's audio, check peaks with ffmpeg volumedetect (max ≤ -1 dB).\nReport: numbered list \"frame · problem · file · fix\" and a verdict: ready / needs fixes.", "example": "COMPOSITION = FinalProject", "preview": null}, {"id": "batch-videos", "ar": "إنتاج فيديوهات بالجملة", "en": "Batch Video Generator", "cat": "dev", "d": "قالب واحد + ملف بيانات = عشرات الفيديوهات بأسماء مختلفة.", "vars": ["TEMPLATE", "DATA_FILE", "NAME_FIELD"], "tools": "Claude Code · Codex · Cursor", "req": "مشروع Remotion شغّال + Skill remotion-best-practices + قالب فيه Zod schema", "text": "Generate one video per row of {{DATA_FILE}} using the template composition {{TEMPLATE}}.\n1. Check the template has a Zod schema; validate every row against it and log invalid rows.\n2. Write scripts/batch.ts using @remotion/bundler (bundle once) and @remotion/renderer (selectComposition + renderMedia per row with inputProps).\n3. Output to out/<{{NAME_FIELD}}>.mp4, skip files that already exist (resume).\n4. Add an npm script \"batch\" and tell me how to run it.", "example": "TEMPLATE = T01-AboutMe · DATA_FILE = data/team.json · NAME_FIELD = slug", "preview": null}]};
